NAME

ulibStoreProductName - Returns the name associated with a FidoNet product code


SYNOPSIS

void ulibStoreProductName(UBYTE *String, long ProductCode)
                                a0              d0


DESCRIPTION

This function stores the name associated with the provided FidoNet product code
<ProductCode>, in the string <String>.

The <String> variable must be able to accomodate up to 64 bytes (63 characters
plus a null terminator).

All 256 product codes have already been allocated names by the FTSC, and
Xenolink is aware of the product names for all 256 (the last two are specified
as "reserved").

Xenolink will supply "Unknown" for unknown product codes, and "Dropped" for
codes which have been officially dropped.

Xenolink's own product code is 170; in the "xenolink.h" include file it is
defined as:

   #define XENOLINK_PRODUCT_CODE 0xAA

(0xAA is hexedecimal for 170).


RETURNS

None
